Line 1: There's no item at position 0.
    say every 0th item of scores
              ^^^
Positions start at 1: "every 2nd item" means items 2, 4, 6 and so on.

Line 2: Something is missing after "to".
    say items 2 to of scores
                ^^
Say where the items end, like "items 2 to 4 of scores" or "items 2 to the end of scores".

Line 3: I expected "of" here, but found "scores".
    say the first 3 items scores
                          ^^^^^^
Write it like "the first 3 items in scores".

Line 4: A position worked out with arithmetic needs parentheses.
    say items n plus 1 to 3 of scores
                ^^^^
Write it like "item (n plus 1) of scores".

Line 5: Something is missing after "without the first".
    say scores without the first
               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Did you mean "without the first item"?

Line 6: I expected "of" here, but found "scores".
    say every second item scores
                          ^^^^^^
Write it like "every second item of scores".
